Cross-reference — DIS-01 Rev 4 §3.6 (Controlled-capacity recognition)	
A limit below nameplate is recognized only with a valid UL 1741 / UL 3141 PCS certification plus an approved Control Narrative — sufficient in themselves for recognition. Where the site's arrangement includes utility equipment, the recognized limit is enforced as applicable: telemetry monitoring, and on pure-generation sites the POI recloser's ANSI 32 directional-power element set to the recognized limit and tripping on violation.	
How to use this list	
The Inverters tab lists smart-inverter models with a valid UL 1741-SB certification of record as of the edition date, together with quarterly-addendum listings whose certification became final during the edition's active period. The Power Control Systems tab lists UL 3141-certified PCS assemblies eligible to satisfy the controlled-capacity recognition path under DIS-01 §3.6. Listing on this edition does not by itself authorize interconnection; project-specific screening, protection, and commissioning requirements continue to apply. Models delisted, discontinued, or with certifications not renewed between quarterly editions are removed from succeeding editions; historical records are retained by Standards Engineering.	
Change summary since CEL-2024-Q3	
— 9 inverter models added on new UL 1741-SB certifications received 08/2024–10/2024.	
— 2 inverter models removed (manufacturer discontinued line).	
— Selvix SV-720 added on receipt of UL 1741-SB certification (initial listing).	
— Quenda Controls QC-PCS-500 and QC-PCS-1000 added on UL 3141 certification (initial PCS listings).	
